            <ArticleTitle>Side-branch wire entrapment during bifurcation PCI: avoidance and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>351-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22269</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An LAD/D1 bifurcation intervention was complicated by side-branch wire entrapment and unravelling requiring goose-neck snare removal. Residual microfilaments were retrieved from the main branch after further balloon inflations with a satisfactory final angiographic result and one-year follow-up. Various methods are available to avoid and deal with this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
